86045417] [17592186129995 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129998 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129998 #edb/ref 1061 21042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129998 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4d3e2ed9-de76-5074-a0bb-abe21e14e37a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129998 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130000 #edb/ref 1061 21046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130000 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c29b2bea-ed1e-5b20-9cc3-069e498275d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130000 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130009 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130009 #edb/ref 1061 21305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130009 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0aa23958-fdd5-54a2-be1c-4973f90a46b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130009 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130184 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130184 #edb/ref 1061 37429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130184 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9826454e-71bd-5e12-b748-06f49a3ff03f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130184 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130363 #edb/ref 1064 "It's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph. We summarize all possible cases in the table below:\n\n| Multiplicity | Case 1 | Case 2 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ \n\n (Simple root) \n\n Odd | ![](images/5a/5a0221f93c65a1eeb4503604a558a6da81c4c7af81c2c52cc35ecf3d189fe99f.png) | ![](images/d5/d556b4edf39181eebb7ec87c344d6f657a6875ecd2745405eaf5351ccaff6f96.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple root) \n\n Even | ![](images/9d/9d14c2588da2ee9c9f5bbc32a70791146bed609ea0d6d5912aeaa2edab02e2d7.png) | ![](images/28/28ad9248a9a509e3a44937d0438fb2366f550a22360d01b9b6a29bcac41357e8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple root) \n\n Odd | ![](images/3a/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](images/95/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The graph is **tangent** to the $x$-axis at multiple roots. This means that if $x=a$ is a multiple root, then the graph of the polynomial is parallel to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- If the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a.$\n\n- If the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd* (including a simple root of multiplicity $1$), the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a.$\n\n- The graph of the polynomial is *never* tangent to the $x$-axis at simple roots." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130363 #edb/ref 1065 3755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130363 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7d750148-b50a-541e-99a4-c4dcd72534bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130363 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324510 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324510 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324510 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "42f76b4e-c2e3-5210-b8b9-db6bc53bafc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325114 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325114 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325114 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "868d64bf-05a4-5a8a-bb2f-f215d1a3fb4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325458 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325458 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325458 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aefcef1a-2486-5ad4-889b-d4796ad4702f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325924 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325924 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325924 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dfae7751-a48a-56fb-8fe9-dabe433a0205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326205 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326205 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326205 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd71fe36-ab9d-5173-8340-e63507c5a1eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186324510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186325924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186326205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186325114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326541 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b1d289fa-530e-56e8-81da-88ee4282c3b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326713 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326713 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38770" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326713 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326713 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/cd/cd19717bd41b787346a96394ce3bc4e38fe690340bb73bd3d11139d41ff977e2.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $x=2$ is a simple root.\n\nII. $x=-1$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n\nIII. $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326713 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fbe22a70-053f-5354-8d7b-dc32dacb2db4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326713 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=2$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=-1$  has an even multiplicity because at $x=-1$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement III is false. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345736 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345736 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345736 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b75e759-23b9-5a00-8a2f-7c0ca516d97a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346616 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346616 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346616 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "910cdafc-67fc-587c-87f0-bdba48190064" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346950 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346950 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346950 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b75eed07-3b22-5842-aac1-37ec3c1762bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347019 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347019 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347019 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c106e615-06ca-5d4a-9046-a19b20c78b0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347213 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347213 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347213 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d48896a5-f655-5550-962f-afc68a851fd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186346616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347910 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b0b44f15-bb40-5519-8a0c-c8353afc8e01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348357 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348357 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80303" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348357 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348357 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0a/0a7b19b50822235a2dcbfcdf74984735a1e26b2b775180b24bdc2bcbf24c588b.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $x=-2$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n\nII. $x=1$ is **not** a simple root.\n\nIII. $x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348357 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9e0f13e6-ba4b-56eb-b269-f07bb6ae2732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348357 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-2$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=-2$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=1$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=1$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
